From e2dcc9312e7cd1ad8edf74b5d320f53848f6c084 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolai Protasov <nprotaso@amd.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:52:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] [AMD] Route Qwen3.8's 512-expert softmax router through
 AITER topk_gating

fused_topk has no ASM router for 512 experts with top-10, while AITER's
topk_gating has an E=512 kernel. Use it on gfx950 for BF16 hidden sizes 2560
(Qwen3.8-Flash-Next) and 8192 (Qwen3.8) up to 4096 rows, without a
correction bias, fused shared experts or packed output, when topk_gating
honors need_renorm for softmax. SGLANG_ROCM_USE_AITER_TOPK_GATING=0 keeps
fused_topk.

From amd-nprotaso/sglang qwen_3_8_improvement: 92e3addcd1.
